From: llmc RK3588 target
Subject: [PATCH] rocket: export affinity helpers used by ggml backend

The current ggml-rocket dequant worker pool asks librocketnpu for the
detected big-core count and pins each persistent worker through the
library's existing affinity policy.  rocket-userspace implements the
pinning helper, but neither exports its declaration nor implements the
count accessor.  This makes the documented sibling-source and installed
package builds fail.

Keep detection in one place and expose the two scheduling-only helpers.
They do not change numerical behavior.
---
 include/rocket_npu.h  | 9 +++++++++
 src/rocket_affinity.c | 6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/rocket_npu.h b/include/rocket_npu.h
--- a/include/rocket_npu.h
+++ b/include/rocket_npu.h
@@ -83,6 +83,15 @@ int  rocket_open(void);
  * with the default 0 (or never calling it) preserves the historical behaviour. */
 void rocket_affinity_set_base(int base);
 int  rocket_affinity_get_base(void);
+
+/* Return the number of performance-cluster CPUs selected by the same affinity
+ * policy used by the matmul workers. Zero means affinity pinning is disabled or
+ * the machine has no distinct performance cluster. */
+int  rocket_num_big_cores(void);
+
+/* Pin one worker through the library's detected/overridden big-core rotation.
+ * This is a scheduling hint only and does not alter any tensor values. */
+void rocket_pin_worker(int worker_idx);
 
 /* ============================================================================
  * SECTION — Buffer allocation, cache management & fence polling
diff --git a/src/rocket_affinity.c b/src/rocket_affinity.c
--- a/src/rocket_affinity.c
+++ b/src/rocket_affinity.c
@@ -133,6 +133,12 @@ static void detect_once(void)
     }
 }
 
+int rocket_num_big_cores(void)
+{
+    pthread_once(&g_once, detect_once);
+    return g_n_big > 0 ? g_n_big : 0;
+}
+
 /* ============================================================================
  * SECTION — Worker pinning
  * ==========================================================================*/
